# Build After Implementation

After finishing an implementation (code edits that can affect compile), verify with a CLI build before considering the task done.

## Command

From `ios/`:

```bash
xcodebuild -scheme AapVitality -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' build
```

Request unrestricted permissions when needed so Xcode/simulator services work.

## CLI scope

- **Build only** — do not terminate, install, launch, or run the app on a simulator/device via CLI unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not use `simctl terminate`, `simctl install`, `simctl launch`, or `xcodebuild` with a run/test action by default.
- The user runs and tests in Xcode or the Simulator themselves.

## When to run

- After implementing or fixing Swift/iOS code
- After resolving build errors
- Before telling the user the work is complete

## When to skip

- Pure docs, rules, or non-code changes
- The user explicitly asks not to build
- Only exploring/reading code with no edits

## On failure

- Fix compile errors and rebuild
- Report remaining failures clearly if blocked
